      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        171.3824005126953,
        527.4089965820312,
        185.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "Options for TB diagnosis recommended by WHO comprise two broad groups: i) initial tests for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        185.3824005126953,
        527.425537109375,
        199.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "diagnosing TB, often including at least rifampicin resistance detection, and ii) follow-on tests used",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.3824005126953,
        527.4235229492188,
        213.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "after TB confirmation to detect additional drug resistance. These guidelines focus on the first",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        213.3824005126953,
        527.4200439453125,
        227.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "category. Table 2.6 summarizes the initial WHO-recommended rapid diagnostic tests for TB, which",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.3824005126953,
        527.4168701171875,
        241.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "are applicable for everyone, except LF-LAM and the use of mWRD in blood which are specific to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        241.3824005126953,
        527.3816528320312,
        255.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "people living with HIV. Further details on the accuracy of all the tests as well as the follow-on tests",
